  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: 
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: "A traveller from far, far south saw a chef serving
    this to a customer, mistaking it for a dish from his culture. He exclaimed that
    he was proud to see 'pilaf' so far from home, and wanted to see the chef cook
    it to compare it to his family's recipe. \"It\u2019s amazing how many of those
    small things crawl out when you are grilling the meat. They writhe and squirm,
    and if you listen carefully, you can hear the hundreds of white worms screaming
    in pain,\" the chef said, a proud smile splitting his face in half as the sound
    of the huge cleaver coming down on the vegetables shook the travellers soul.
    \"Or\u2026.. that might be the sizzling oil,\" he continued as he threw the vegetables
    into the pan. The traveller turned around and ran. He ran and ran and kept on
    running, and did not stop until he was miles outside of Aijinkova."
